---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Monitoring Automation | ORASOLU"
  description="Practical resources for turning database checks into repeatable monitoring and operational workflows."
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · AUTOMATION &amp; DEVOPS</div>
        <h1>Monitoring Automation</h1>
        <p>
          Practical resources for turning database checks into repeatable monitoring and operational workflows.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · AUTOMATION &amp; DEVOPS</div>
          <h2>Turn database checks into useful signals</h2>
          <p>
            Monitoring automation works best when each check has a clear threshold, useful evidence and an operational response. These examples provide simple starting points for repeatable database monitoring.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">01 · SESSIONS</div>
              <h2>Monitor active sessions</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Identify sessions currently active or waiting so workload changes can be surfaced.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    sid,
    serial#,
    username,
    status,
    event,
    wait_class,
    seconds_in_wait
FROM v$session
WHERE type = 'USER'
ORDER BY seconds_in_wait DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">02 · TABLESPACE</div>
              <h2>Monitor tablespace usage</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Identify tablespaces whose used percentage has reached a monitoring threshold.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    tablespace_name,
    ROUND(used_percent, 2) AS used_percent
FROM dba_tablespace_usage_metrics
WHERE used_percent &gt;= 80
ORDER BY used_percent DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">03 · BLOCKING</div>
              <h2>Monitor blocking sessions</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Find sessions currently blocking other sessions.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    sid,
    serial#,
    username,
    blocking_session,
    event
FROM v$session
WHERE blocking_session IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY blocking_session, sid;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">04 · INVALID</div>
              <h2>Monitor invalid objects</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Detect invalid objects that may indicate deployment or maintenance issues.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    owner,
    object_type,
    COUNT(*) AS invalid_count
FROM dba_objects
WHERE status = 'INVALID'
GROUP BY owner, object_type
ORDER BY invalid_count DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">05 · JOBS</div>
              <h2>Monitor scheduler failures</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Surface recent scheduler failures for operational follow-up.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    owner,
    job_name,
    status,
    error#,
    actual_start_date
FROM dba_scheduler_job_run_details
WHERE status &lt;&gt; 'SUCCEEDED'
ORDER BY actual_start_date DESC
FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">06 · ALERTS</div>
              <h2>Build a monitoring result</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Return a simple status value that can be consumed by a script or monitoring workflow.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    CASE
        WHEN EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM dba_tablespace_usage_metrics
            WHERE used_percent &gt;= 90
        )
        THEN 'ALERT'
        ELSE 'OK'
    END AS status
FROM dual;</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <div class="resource-note__label">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · AUTOMATION &amp; DEVOPS</div>
          <h3>A monitoring check should lead to useful evidence.</h3>
          <p>
            Avoid collecting metrics without an operational purpose. Define what is being checked, what threshold matters and what evidence an operator needs when the check reports a problem.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/automation/">
            Back to Automation &amp; DevOps
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";

    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>

<style>
.resource-section {
  padding-top: 56px;
  padding-bottom: 72px;
}

.resource-intro {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}

.resource-intro h2 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.resource-intro p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.resource-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 22px;
  align-items: start;
}

.resource-block {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  height: 560px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 30px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: #ffffff;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  transition:
    border-color 0.22s ease,
    box-shadow 0.22s ease,
    transform 0.22s ease;
}

.resource-block:hover {
  border-color: #d8dce1;
  box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
  transform: translateY(-3px);
}

.resource-block__header {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.resource-block__label {
  margin-bottom: 9px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.2;
}

.resource-block h2 {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.resource-block__description {
  min-height: 48px;
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}

.resource-block pre {
  position: relative;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 22px;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overflow-y: auto;
  background: #2f353d;
  border-radius: 10px;
  color: #f3f4f6;
  font-family:
    "Cascadia Code",
    "Consolas",
    "Courier New",
    monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.7;
  white-space: pre;
}

.resource-block code {
  font-family: inherit;
  white-space: pre;
}

.resource-copy-button {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  right: 10px;
  padding: 5px 9px;
  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #374151;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  cursor: pointer;
  z-index: 2;
}

.resource-copy-button:hover {
  background: #f3f4f6;
}

.resource-note {
  margin-top: 32px;
  padding: 30px;
  background: #f7f8fa;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
}

.resource-note__label {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
}

.resource-note h3 {
  margin: 0 0 12px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.resource-note p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.resource-actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 24px;
  margin-top: 32px;
}

@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 680px) {
  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 52px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .resource-block {
    height: 520px;
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 0;
  }

  .resource-block pre {
    padding: 18px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .resource-note {
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .resource-actions {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 18px;
  }
}
</style>
